func claim_mapping_adr
  ret "**Which claims Entra ID issues.** One sample claim:

| Claim | Source | Configured as | In |
|---|---|---|---|
| `department` | the user's `department` in Entra ID, editable by administrators only | an optional claim (or a claims-mapping policy) of the app registration | the access token, and the ID token so the frontend can hide what the user may not use (`useHasClaim`) |

Locally, the stand-in issues it from each user's `Department` in `src/IdentityStandIn/appsettings.json`.

**How to add a claim.**

1. Have Entra ID issue it: an optional claim of the API's app registration for the access token (and of the web client's for the ID token, if the frontend should see it), or a claims-mapping policy for an attribute that is not one, and document it in docs/adr.
2. Have the stand-in issue it: a property of `StandInUser`, set as a claim in `TokenIssuer`, and a value for the local users in `src/IdentityStandIn/appsettings.json`.
3. Require it in the module's `<Module>Policies` and test it as `<Module>ClaimTests` does.

The stand-in's settings are development only; production configures the app registration itself."
end
func claim_change_adr
  ret "A new claim is a change in the app registration (an optional claim) and in the stand-in (`StandInUser`, `TokenIssuer`, its users)."
end
func add_claim_rule
  ret "To add a claim: make it an optional claim of the app registration in Entra ID, and have the stand-in issue it (a property of `StandInUser`, set in `TokenIssuer`, and a value for the local users in `src/IdentityStandIn/appsettings.json`)."
end
